The high of <strong>41\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 48\u00b0F, and the record is 63\u00b0F (1909, 1911, 1964, 2012). The low of <strong>32\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Glens Falls' climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Glens Falls has set <strong>89 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 81 that chance alone would give, and <strong>88 record highs</strong>, close to the 81 that chance alone would give. The 1910s hold the most record highs of any decade (46). Glens Falls' all-time high is 101\u00b0F, on July 3, 1911.","t_chg":"Glens Falls' nights show no clear change. Its days have warmed since 1986.","p_chg":"Across 111 complete years: Glens Falls' average low shows no clear change: \u22120.03\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.10 to +0.05) that includes zero. Glens Falls' average high shows no clear change: +0.05\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.02 to +0.12) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows show no clear change and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.56\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.21 to +0.90). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 3 months fell. Highs rose in 3 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Glens Falls' yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.11 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 38.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1983 (54.40 in); the driest, 1964 (21.76 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 4 daily record highs, 4 daily record lows"}}